= Thermodynamics — Simple =

'''Thermodynamics''' is the science of heat, work and how energy moves through systems.

One important rule is that energy is not created or destroyed in a closed, complete energy account. Heating something adds energy to it; if it does work while heating or expanding, some energy may leave that way.

Another rule limits what changes can happen naturally. Heat normally flows from warmer objects to cooler ones unless work is used to move it the other way, as in a refrigerator.

Thermodynamics helps explain engines, air conditioners, weather and many chemical reactions.

